 - Only managers may delete tasks.
 - Archived projects reject all writes with 409 (reads still work).
 - A task ID that does not belong to the project in the path → 404.
+- Removing a user from an organization (`DELETE /orgs/{orgID}/users/{uid}`)
+  is for org admins of that organization only. Another organization → 404;
+  a non-admin member → 403. The target user must belong to that organization,
+  otherwise 404; a user with no memberships there gets 204 (the call is
+  idempotent). The user's memberships in all of the org's projects are removed,
+  including archived projects (this is an access removal, so the archived
+  rule does not apply), and the user's task assignments in those projects are
+  cleared. The user record itself is not changed.
 
